  "details": "For PC, both VR and Desktop users you could be unfortunate enough like me to come across this bug that no matter what you do, will always prevent you from loading worlds past 0.00%. The only exception to this rule are worlds that have already been pre-loaded or have been visited before, prior to the bug occurring. However, attempting to clear the cache will result in the user being thrown into an infinite loop of the 0.00% loading screen as you haven't been to your home world/default world yet since you cleared your cache. The only partial solution to this bug is installing a VPN that will allow for you to load all these things with a cost. With the VPN active you cannot: Load video players of any kind, avatars take anywhere between 5-10 minutes to fully load in, a friend dropping a portal will 9x out of 10 of the time produce an error message for you saying, \"World Owner Access\", meaning you'll have to be invited once they load in on the other side, opening menus or accepting invites or joining off someone will take 5-10 minutes as well, and finally the VPN can produce a lot of lag causing Vrchat to on occasion, break.\n\nThis bug report is not discussing the VPN, but to help give an idea on what i've had to deal with for the past two months. Please fix this!",
